    "lesson": {
      "title": "Genome to organism",
      "instruction": "Create an offspring, or look closer at its inherited information.",
      "explanation": "Fictional diploid organism with three loci in a partial teaching genome; sequence snippets are illustrative. Meiosis and fertilization are distinct from mitosis. Dominance describes the crest trait relationship. Some genes produce functional RNA. Offspring retain parental segment provenance. Parent edits never rewrite existing descendants; germline mutation is explicitly recorded."
